  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. The project has successfully completed its testing phase and achieved its first major milestone ahead of schedule, including the testing of a secure file sharing prototype. The next phase involves user interface enhancements planned for October. Regarding finances, the initial phase one budget was $500,000, which was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. Additionally, specific budgets have been approved for compliance ($55,000) and training ($15,000). The executive board has also approved a total budget of $2 million covering research, development, and marketing. The team is exploring partnership opportunities with TechInnovate for AI technology, and a celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
